    "body": "The ROCm draft I am preparing is materially different from #49323 and #42765: those fixes use stride-two even/odd loads and stores, while this version uses contiguous I/O with register-only split/interleave and a bounded one-wave ROCm launch for small adjacent-pair tiles. On MI355 it remains bit-exact, passes the 24 MRoPE GPU cases and four GLM compile cases, and is faster than the former incorrect layout at the tested prefill sizes.",
