    "created_at": "2026-07-28T17:53:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-07-28T17:53:37Z",
    "body": "> The ROCm draft I am preparing is materially different from [#49323](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/49323) and [#42765](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/42765): those fixes use stride-two even/odd loads and stores, while this version uses contiguous I/O with register-only split/interleave and a bounded one-wave ROCm launch for small adjacent-pair tiles. On MI355 it remains bit-exact, passes the 24 MRoPE GPU cases and four GLM compile cases, and is faster than the former incorrect layout at the tested prefill sizes.\n\nthe fix has landed upstream in [#49906] (adapted from the proposal in #49323). Closing this as resolved. Thanks @AndreasKaratzas for the review and the additional AMD-side improvements!",
